* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Flame, not lame-add-on.wav|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|sometimes|attributive}} Something which can be appended to something else.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1969|author=Edward D. Giacomini|title=California Retail Installment Sales|page=172
|passage=Payments made before an '''add-on''' sale must be allocated entirely to the previous contract or contracts.}}
# {{lb|en|computer hardware|software}} A [[software]] extension or [[hardware]] [[peripheral]] that provides additional functions or customization for a core application or system.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2010|author=Kenneth Baldauf; Ralph Stair|title=Succeeding with Technology|page=77
|passage=Microdrives that can hold several gigabytes (see Figure 2.20) have been available as '''add-ons''' for portable devices.}}
# {{lb|en|poker}} Additional [[chip]]s that can be [[purchase]]d at specific times in tournament play.
# {{lb|en|video games}} {{synonym of|en|expansion pack}}.

